@startuml
title Proof of Collaboration (PoCol) Consensus Round with Unused Nonce Space Due to Inactive Miner
skinparam dpi 180
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
participant "Miner A (active miner)" as A
participant "Miner B (active miner)" as B
participant "Miner C (inactive miner)" as C
participant "Blockchain ledger" as L

A -> A: Read current registered miner set from the local blockchain ledger\n(for example: Miner A, Miner B, Miner C)
B -> B: Read current registered miner set from the local blockchain ledger\n(the same set of Miner A, Miner B, Miner C)
C -> C: Read current registered miner set from the local blockchain ledger\n(the same set of Miner A, Miner B, Miner C)
A -> A: Build candidate block header for this round\nfrom the local mempool of Miner A and from the hash of the previous block
B -> B: Build candidate block header for this round\nfrom the local mempool of Miner B and from the hash of the previous block
C -> C: Build candidate block header for this round\nfrom the local mempool of Miner C and from the hash of the previous block
A -> A: Apply the Proof of Collaboration nonce distribution function\nusing the previous block hash, the candidate block header,\nthe current round number, the maximum nonce value,\nand the shared registered miner set to compute:\n(1) a pseudo-random but deterministic ordered list of all registered miners,\n(2) the index of Miner A in this ordered list,\n(3) the start and end of the nonce range assigned to Miner A
B -> B: Apply the same nonce distribution function\nusing the same public inputs to compute:\n(1) the same ordered list of registered miners,\n(2) the index of Miner B in this ordered list,\n(3) the start and end of the nonce range assigned to Miner B
C -> C: Apply the same nonce distribution function\nusing the same public inputs to compute:\n(1) the same ordered list of registered miners,\n(2) the index of Miner C in this ordered list,\n(3) the start and end of the nonce range assigned to Miner C
A -> A: Start the Proof of Work search by repeatedly computing\ncryptographic hashes of the candidate block header combined with nonce values\nfrom the nonce range assigned to Miner A and comparing each hash value\nwith the difficulty target
B -> B: Start the Proof of Work search by repeatedly computing\ncryptographic hashes of the candidate block header combined with nonce values\nfrom the nonce range assigned to Miner B and comparing each hash value\nwith the difficulty target
C -> C: Remain inactive and do not compute cryptographic hashes\nfor nonce values in the nonce range assigned to Miner C;\nthis part of the nonce space is not explored in this round
A -> A: If a nonce value is found such that the cryptographic hash\nof the candidate block header combined with this nonce value\nis below the difficulty target, construct a new block that contains\nthe candidate block header, the winning nonce value,\nand the selected transactions
A -> A: Compute reward share for each registered miner\naccording to the Proof of Collaboration reward distribution function\n(for example, based on equal shares or a chosen collaboration metric)\nNote: the reward distribution may still include the inactive Miner C\nif Miner C is part of the registered miner set in this round
A -> A: Create reward outputs in the new block so that the block reward\nand the transaction fees are distributed among all registered miners\n(for example, separate outputs for Miner A, Miner B, and Miner C)
A -> B: Broadcast new block with winning nonce value\nand distributed reward outputs to Miner B
A -> C: Broadcast new block with winning nonce value\nand distributed reward outputs to Miner C\n(if Miner C is still online as a node but not participating in mining)
B -> B: Verify validity of the received block, including proof of work,\nvalidity of all transactions, correctness of the nonce range used by Miner A\naccording to the nonce distribution function,\nand correctness of the reward distribution among all registered miners
C -> C: Verify validity of the received block, including proof of work,\nvalidity of all transactions, correctness of the nonce range used by Miner A,\nand correctness of the reward distribution among all registered miners
A -> A: Verify the constructed block again for consistency\nbefore committing it to the local blockchain ledger
A -> L: Append the new valid block for this round\nto the local view of the blockchain ledger of Miner A
B -> L: Append the new valid block for this round\nto the local view of the blockchain ledger of Miner B
C -> L: Append the new valid block for this round\nto the local view of the blockchain ledger of Miner C
A -> A: Remove all transactions that were included in the new block\nfrom the local mempool of Miner A
B -> B: Remove all transactions that were included in the new block\nfrom the local mempool of Miner B
C -> C: Remove all transactions that were included in the new block\nfrom the local mempool of Miner C
A -> A: If all nonce values in the nonce range of Miner A are exhausted\nwithout finding a hash below the difficulty target,\nmark the search over the assigned nonce range of Miner A as completed
B -> B: If all nonce values in the nonce range of Miner B are exhausted\nwithout finding a hash below the difficulty target,\nmark the search over the assigned nonce range of Miner B as completed
C -> C: The nonce range of Miner C remains unexplored\nbecause Miner C is inactive in this round
A -> A: Construct a new candidate block header\n(for example, by updating the timestamp or the set of included transactions)\nand start a new Proof of Collaboration round with this new header
B -> B: Construct the same new candidate block header\nusing the same modification rule and prepare to start the new round
C -> C: Optionally construct the same new candidate block header\nif still participating as a node, even if remaining inactive as a miner
@enduml
